I am back at my desk.
I open the laptop and start.
Jonas fetches a chair for himself.
We have already been programming together for two hours.
"Have you connected the database?" Jonas asks.
"Yes, I already connected it this morning," I answer.
We test the code, but there is an error.
The program crashes immediately.
"Oh no, why didn't that work?" I ask.
Jonas looks closely at the screen.
"Did you save the code?" he asks, laughing.
I check my last line.
"No, I completely forgot to do that!" I say.
As developers, we unfortunately make this mistake often.
I save the file and we try it again.
Now everything works perfectly.
We have solved the first problem.
